IMPORT prelude

-- Land Tax Act 1936 (SA) and Taxation Administration Act 1996 (SA) -- shared nouns for the seat-neutral core.
--
-- SOURCE. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, sourced through the Open Australian Legal
-- Corpus: "Sourced from the South Australian Legislation website at 10 March 2025. For the latest information on South
-- Australian Government legislation, please go to www.legislation.sa.gov.au/." State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0;
-- corpus by Umar Butler / Isaacus, version 7.1.0, CC BY 4.0. Not the official text. The Land Tax Act text is the
-- version of 2023-07-01 (scraped 2024-09-13); the Taxation Administration Act text is the version of 2019-10-03 (scraped
-- 2024-09-13). The Current Titles list of 22 September 2026 lists both at 4.12.2025, so both are out of date. See
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md and NOTES.md.
--
-- Land Tax Act s 3: "This Act should be read together with the Taxation Administration Act 1996 which makes provision for
-- the administration and enforcement of this Act and other taxation laws." TAA s 4(d) makes the Land Tax Act a taxation
-- law. So the parties and acts of both Acts are declared once here.
--
-- This module holds arithmetic and date helpers, the explicit "not covered" answers, and the parties and acts of the
-- regulative rules. It states no rule of either Act.
--
-- Conventions. A financial year is named by the calendar year in which it ENDS: 2023/2024 is 2024. Money is in dollars.
-- Percentages are numbers out of 100.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Shared nouns -- Land Tax Act 1936 and Taxation Administration Act 1996 (SA)`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- Schedule 1 charges "$0.50 for every $100 or fractional part of $100 over Threshold A": a part of $100 counts as a whole
-- $100.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of 100-dollar parts in` MEANS
    IF `amount` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES 100 EQUALS `amount`
         THEN `amount` DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 1

-- Land Tax Act s 8A(8): "the thresholds will be rounded to the nearest $1 000 (with an amount of $500 rounded up)".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest 1000 dollars` MEANS
    FLOOR ((`amount` PLUS 500) DIVIDED BY 1000) TIMES 1000

-- TAA s 26(2)(a): the market rate is an average "rounding up 0.005 to 2 decimal places".
GIVEN `rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to 2 decimal places, 0.005 up` MEANS
    FLOOR (`rate` TIMES 100 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `Dates`

-- Dates are DATE values. The prelude has no ordering on DATE, so days are compared by their serial numbers.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD `y` `m` `d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `last` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `first` `to` `last` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `last` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `first`

-- "12 months after" a day: the same day and month a year later. READING: 29 February is taken to 28 February (the Acts
-- do not say).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `n`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `n`)

-- A financial year runs from 1 July to 30 June and is named by the year in which it ends.
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the financial year` MEANS YMD `the financial year` 6 30

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the financial year` MEANS YMD (`the financial year` MINUS 1) 7 1

§§ `Answers outside the deposited text`

-- Where a question reaches a figure the deposited texts do not contain, the answer says so.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the assessment year is before 2020/2021: Schedule 1 (inserted from 1 July 2020) has no scale for it, and the earlier scales are not in the deposited text`
    `the thresholds for the assessment year were not supplied: the Commissioner publishes them by Gazette notice (s 8A(7)), and the s 8A(2a), (3) and (3b) formulas are missing from the deposited text`
    `the thresholds supplied are not in ascending order (Threshold A, B, C, D)`
    `the s 9(8) deduction was not supplied: its formula is missing from the deposited text`

DECLARE `Land tax answer` IS ONE OF
    `the land tax, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the parties and the acts`

-- The parties the two Acts name. The Commissioner of State Taxation and the Minister are parties to rules, never seats.
DECLARE `Land tax party` IS ONE OF
    `the owner given the exemption notice`
    `the taxpayer`
    `the objector`
    `the Minister`
    `the Commissioner`

-- TAA s 88(4): the Minister may "confirm or revoke the assessment or decision" or "make an assessment or decision in
-- place of" it. What matters to the objector (s 92(a): "dissatisfied with the Minister's determination") is how far the
-- objection succeeded. READING: an objector whose objection is allowed in full is taken not to be dissatisfied.
DECLARE `Objection outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the objection is allowed in full`
    `the objection is allowed in part only`
    `the objection is disallowed`

DECLARE `Land tax act` IS ONE OF
    `notify the Commissioner of the error or inaccuracy in the exemption notice`
    `pay the land tax specified in the assessment` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister, stating the grounds fully and in detail`
    `give written notice of the determination of the objection, with reasons` HAS `outcome` IS AN `Objection outcome`
    `appeal to the Supreme Court`
    `give the Commissioner written notice of the intention to appeal`
    `pay the penalty tax`
